# func/text/tx_char (id 317): CHAR / UNICHAR core, one step. A = number or error; N0 = 0 CHAR, 1 UNICHAR.
# n = TRUNC(A.PAY) (clamped to +-2^23 first). CHAR: 1 <= n <= 255, Windows-1252 (128..159 mapped to
# their Unicode code points), else #VALUE!. UNICHAR: 1 <= n <= 1114111, else #VALUE!; surrogate code
# points 55296..57343 give #N/A; n >= 65536 gives a surrogate pair (2 units).
# Always mem_op 3 (K = 64); N = 3 when valid: block write [length, 1, packed word] at HT, A = (2, HT), HT += 3. Return (LR, LP).
# Note: weights/func/text/tx_char.md
